 "audit": "Diagnosis labels are heterogeneous and overlapping (NOS, Glioma malignant vs Glioblastoma, RMS NOS vs embryonal/alveolar; 'missing'/'Unknown' labels), so one-vs-rest comparisons mix subtypes. 20 hypermutated cases (up to 9075 mutated genes, mostly malignant glioma) were excluded from testing. protein_change values often have impossible positions (e.g. NOTCH2 p.E127469G), so they are unreliable and I could not use them to confirm hotspots or flag artefacts. NOTCH2 in ERMS, MED12 in ependymoma and NF2 in pilocytic astrocytoma are statistically strong but biologically unexpected with no recurrent variants, so they may be technical, batch or pooling artefacts; I gave them low probability. Large genes (TTN, MUC16) were not claimed. Small subtypes give unstable estimates, and the cohort mixes projects with possibly different pipelines.",
 "methods": "Per-case gene mutation presence (any non-synonymous variant). Excluded cases with >150 mutated genes. For each diagnosis with n>=5 and each gene mutated in >=3 cases, ran a one-vs-rest two-sided Fisher exact test (own implementation) and ranked by p with BH-style q. Selected findings with strong significance, large effect and biological plausibility, and set probabilities from significance, effect size, prior literature and artefact concerns."
}